---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { AgentAvatarGallery, AgentAvatarSizes } from '../../components/AgentAvatarDemo';
import { AgentCompositions } from '../../components/AvatarDemo';
---

<Docs title="Agent Avatar" description="Built-in artwork for agents: 100 objects in eight colors.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Agent Avatar</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A picture for each agent, chosen from its id. 100 hand-drawn objects in eight colors ship inside the package, so
    there is nothing to host and no network request.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <AgentAvatarSizes client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Agent avatar"
      code={`import { AgentAvatar } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/agent-avatar";

<AgentAvatar agentId={agent.id} name={agent.name} size="sm" />`}
    />
    <p>
      The same <code>agentId</code> always gets the same object and color. <code>size</code> matches
      <code>Avatar</code>: <code>"xs"</code>, <code>"sm"</code>, <code>"default"</code>, or <code>"lg"</code>. Pass
      <code>object</code> or <code>color</code> to choose the artwork yourself, or <code>src</code> to use your own
      image. With <code>src</code>, the first letter of <code>name</code> shows while it loads or if it fails.
    </p>
    <p>
      The artwork is an inline SVG <code>data:</code> URL, so it renders on the server and works offline. All 100
      objects add about 25 kB gzipped to the <code>agent-avatar</code> entry. Import it from its own entry so other
      avatars stay small.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Gallery</h2>
    <AgentAvatarGallery client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Helpers</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Agent avatar helpers"
      code={`import {
  agentAvatar, agentAvatarArtwork, agentAvatarColors, agentAvatarObjects, agentAvatarSrc,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/agent-avatar";

agentAvatar("agent_123");          // { object: "…", color: "…", src: "data:image/svg+xml,…" }
agentAvatarSrc("agent_123");       // the same src
agentAvatarArtwork("tulip", "pink"); // one object in one color`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>agentAvatarObjects</code> and <code>agentAvatarColors</code> list every choice. Their order is frozen:
      changing it would give existing agents new pictures.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">In context</h2>
    <AgentCompositions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The artwork is decorative and has <code>alt=""</code>. Put the agent's name in nearby text. Avatars are not
      focusable; put them inside a link or button for actions.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
